  "id": "fundamental-need",
  "term": "fundamental need",
  "definition": "In social psychology, a fundamental need is a basic human requirement essential to well-being. In this source, it refers to the need to belong: when this need is met it is linked to better mental and physical health, and when it is blocked it can produce social distress.",
